  "notes": "Modified cash basis (governmental) / accrual (business-type). Governmental receipts and disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); beginning/ending cash = governmental fund balances 351,483 / 354,310 (p4; no liabilities, all cash, CDs and county treasurer cash). Transfers net to zero in the Total column; recorded in 70,000 / out 70,000 from fund columns. Business-type from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p6, Total column); nonoperating interest and bond fees included in disbursements. Statement of Cash Flows (p7) prints only the Water Fund, and the report is cash basis, so proprietary is null. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1, Total) because governmental activities include capital assets (governmental funds balance sheet 354,310 differs from 668,555). Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p11, more detailed than the p8 budget schedule, which is therefore not recorded; only the Law enforcement budget 28,000 maps one-to-one); Street (p9) and Sales Tax (p10) budget schedules. Street Fund capital outlay budget 17,000 with no actual not recorded. No proprietary fund schedules, so no business-type detail. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
